If Amy wins 3/8 of the time and Lily wins 3/10 of the time, then the remaining fraction of the time must be the fraction of ties.
The total fraction of the time is 1, so we have 1 - (3/8) - (3/10) = 1 - 15/40 - 12/40 = 1 - 27/40 = 13/40.
Therefore, the fraction of the time that they tie is $\boxed{\frac{13}{40}}$.The answer is: \frac{13}{40}

To find the decimal expansion of $8/11$, we perform long division:

$$
\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{.} & 7 & 2 & 7 & 2 & 7 & \dots \\
\cline{2-8}
11 & 8 & . & 0 & 9 & 0 & 9 & \dots \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{7} & 0 \\
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 3 & 0 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 2 & 7 \\
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 2 & 3 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & 2 & 2 \\
\cline{5-6}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 8 & \dots \\
\end{array}
$$

We see that the remainder of each division is the same: 8. This means that the decimal expansion of $8/11$ is a repeating decimal with a repeating block of length 2, which consists of the digits 2 and 7. Therefore, the least number of digits in a repeating block of $8/11$ is $\boxed{2}$.

The answer is: 2

