solution_steps:
By AM-GM,
\begin{align*}
\frac{a}{2b} + \frac{b}{4c} + \frac{c}{8a} &\ge 3\sqrt[3]{\frac{a}{2b} \cdot \frac{b}{4c} \cdot \frac{c}{8a}} \\
&= 3\sqrt[3]{\frac{1}{64}} \\
&= 3 \cdot \frac{1}{4} \\
&= \frac{3}{4}.
\end{align*}
Equality occurs when $a = 2b,$ $b = 4c,$ and $c = 8a,$ or $a = \frac{1}{64},$ $b = \frac{1}{32},$ and $c = \frac{1}{16},$ so the minimum value is $\boxed{\frac{3}{4}}$.
The answer is: \frac{3}{4}

